x86_64-linux  The C1 and D1 forms of the specialization's constructors and destructors, and nothing else: clang emits only the base-object C2 and D2 forms of a class template specialization's constructor on this target whether the definition is written inside the class or outside it - measured here with every one written outside - and cxx1 emits the complete-object forms beside them, the difference move-constructor.nonames records. Every C2 and D2 name agrees; arm64-darwin agrees on all 17 names and x86_64-windows on all 10.
